{
  "version": 2,
  "description": "Per-exam paper layout table. A layout entry is [SUBJECT, from, to] over the GLOBAL ORDINAL position of a question inside the paper. The ordinal is (index in the paper's questions[] array + 1): the source `n` field restarts at 1 for every section, so it is NOT a paper position. 'layout_rules' are evaluated in order, first match wins; a rule may filter on 'years' and/or 'length' (questions in the paper). 'detect': true means the layout must be derived per paper from its own section structure + content keywords (CGL Tier-II non-Paper-I, CHSL Tier-II).",
  "provenance": {
    "note": "Row-by-row section order and section sizes were measured across all 1,322 in-scope papers by splitting each paper at its `n` resets and taking the keyword majority of every section. Where the task-specified table disagrees with the corpus, the corpus value is used and the difference is documented in docs/DATA_MODEL.md and _meta/coverage.md.",
    "measured_corrections": [
      "CGL Tier-II Paper-I is 30/30/45/25/20 = MATH, REAS, ENG, GK, COMPUTER (not 30/30/30/30/30).",
      "CHSL Tier-I switched from ENG,REAS,MATH,GK to REAS,GK,MATH,ENG for the 2022-23 and 2023 papers.",
      "MTS 2019/2021 order is ENG,REAS,MATH,GK; MTS 2022 is REAS,MATH,ENG,GK; MTS 2023+ (90 questions) is MATH,REAS,GK,ENG with sizes 20/20/25/25.",
      "GD 2019 and 2021 have four 25-question sections and no Hindi section; GD 2022+ has five 20-question sections with Hindi last.",
      "CGL Tier-II 'other' papers (AAO Finance, Statistics/JSO) are single 100-question sections and need per-paper detection."
    ]
  },
  "subjects": ["REAS", "GK", "MATH", "ENG", "COMPUTER", "HINDI"],
